// The forward reference to a later-declared top-level `fn` also resolves inside a `${…}` string
// interpolation hole — the hole merely contains the call, so the top-level fn hoist covers it. This
// is the shape the bug was first noticed in; it is fixed by the same hoist as the plain call.
// expect: stdout "x: hello"
// expect: exit 0
echo "x: ${greet()}"
fn greet(): string {
    return "hello";
}
